tmp_text "1) Who is threatening to remove quests? I didn't see it.2) There is a major difference between being told where to go to start a quest,  and being told how to complete a quest. 3) You cannot justify cheating by saying \"Since I don't know how to do  this quest, I must have someone show me\", which is another way of saying  \"...there are not enough clues\"\"...we are not mind-readers\".4) Any quest I worked on that had a bug, the bug was fixed as soon a   high ranking wiz was aware of the problem.5) What the heck do you mean by passwords? Do you have trouble logging on?There is a difference between a game mud and a social net. This is a game.A game is not fun without a certain amount of challenge. Sure, there isa lot of social interaction here, and I am not knocking that at all, but there is a problem to solve in this game that requires some effort or is no fun.If you can write a quest that is better then the ones here, by all means,do so. If you are apprentice, you will not be always. If you are new,you have everything you need.(Yow! Some of these europeans are better at English then I am!)**I think Saffron was referring to one quest which required you gaining a password, to release an AnySlayer sword.Now, this particular password was misspelt, which makes itincredibly difficult to discover by 'normal' means...	Elemental Tamina**The only time i truely cheated, i got banished for, and by the way, i know that least 50% of wizards have cheated. The thing is, asking for where a person's are is, is technically cheating. There aren't enough hints given. I would like to see someone solve the King Dmitri quest without a hint, the Anyslayer, The island dragon, the wolf quest, etc. I bet $100 you have cheated more than once.**the help hern quest has a \" \" space in it instead of the \"_\"Could this be fixed so that we can adjust players before toomany solve it and it becomes harder to do?-Mangla**Maybe you are right stanley, but since i know of more than 10of our current active wizards who used one of my quest solutionsi recknon i am justified in saying what i said about current wizzesand cheatingTex**Kyoshi quest revised after 10th player solved it.Descriptions cleared up.Tats**Due to the free doom slave quest, I am rewriting my free the slaves uest.Also I am working on a second quest revolving around faeries.Exos**The whale in the ishikawa quest has been made less confusingit was the major stumbling block for most players**I have an idea that might work. As others have saidearilier that many players get frustrated at questing becausethey don't know where to start. A possible idea is to create'A Hall of Learning' where players can learn of places on thegame and have to have basic knowledge of where things are to find the areas as per described. Almost like a book on everywizards area and roughly were it is located or how to go aboutfinding where it is located. If possible can a higher wiz okaythis - it might solve a lot of things/problems on the game.Unsure Ap**I guess no one reads this board!Ap**Untrue...some of us do read the board...Unfortunately, I don't have the power to do much with it...H.**Three minor quests installed for samurai only, no quest pointsawarded, even though two of these are more involved than mostof the quests on the mud.Dine with the Emperor.Appease the Kami.Honor Lord Raiden.Tatsuo**sounds good ap., is always nice to know where to start! :*)**Honor Lord Raiden...I dont remember him leaving my area to become a Samurai..Have to have a talk with that boy... *GRIN*Gumbo**Have a new quest ready, waiting for approval.  Its a quest based on puzzles, and requires no fighting (though there are monsters in the area, it is notnecessary to engage them).  There are 3 puzzles in the quest, each is of moderate difficulty.  THe first is just minesweeper, which isn't so mucha puzzle as it is a game, though there are certain elements of logicnecessary to win.  The second is a puzzle involving 12 coins, one of which is counterfeit and distinguishable only by wieght, and a balancingscale.  The last is a chess-based puzzle involving only the knights and a3x3 board.  None of the puzzles are all that hard, and a file containing the solutions is posted in/players/kawai/areas/games/ as are the rest of the files.  Knowing the solutions, it takes about 10-15 minutes on a slow link (14.4k dialup)to complete the three, since both minesweeper and the chess game relyon visual representations of the board, though if you're good atminesweeper you really don't have too look at the board all that much.The puzzles are coded so that only one person may try at a time, and it does remember where a person left off, so long as they haven't logged off since trying a puzzle...As for players just solving by script, its not really possible, since minesweeper is different each game, and while the chessgame can be played by script, the coin game can not be, since the coinchanges each time (there is, however, a simple solution that can bescripted, with the results compared to a table...requires knowing themathematical proof/solution to the puzzle though...otherwise its left to players ingenuity....)Anyway, I'd appreciate feedback on this quest, whether or not its toodifficult or not.  Also, feel free to debug (though should be fairly bugfree...been in the works for a while as just games to play, thought I'dtry integrating into a quest).  TO enter the area, goto /players/kawai/areas/games/start-K**Just wanted to say, that when I was a player, I thought puzzle quests were absurd, sometimes a waste of time(king dmitri) and does not really fit the flow of the game. Minesweeper is a game anyone can play who has windows, why put it on the mud too?? Just voicing an opinion,Tanis**Why don't puzzles fit the flow of the game?  Experience is supposed tobe a combination of physical development as well as mental development, andlogic games have been around since people started thinking.  Besides, whyadd another quest that just requires killing a bunch of monsters, whichis what most of the quests on here are.  non-killing quests alsoallow low-level players to accomplish somewhat challenging questswithout fear of death and such.  It just seems that right nowthe quests are easy really easy or require tremendous amounts of killing, few quests in between....As for minesweeper, that doesn't necessarily have to be part of the quest,its just there becuase I happened to have it coded at the time...there areplenty of other puzzles to put in, and after time the quest can changeby substituting new puzzles (even just pick randomly from a library of puzzlI just happened to like minsweeper because it varies, and playerscan't script solutions to the quest, which is a problem around here.-K-  -Who thinks guilds/combat have gotten way out of hand\\**Players are really tired of solving puzzles while they don't get enuf infoson quests. Why should they care of these stupid puzzles...? Just check out thegannja puzzle no wizs can actually think that this one is really enjoyable.ThormPS: Once again , quests should be difficult and hard to figure out BUT theystill have to be LOGICAL, and ENJOYABLE. :)**The reason you guys dislike puzzles is that you cannot cheat onthem like every other on - get over it you are wizzes now and youshould care about what types of quests are good or not - we are tryingto stop the immense amount of cheating that has hit holy mission withsome great force - some quests that soltions have been out on aredone every time it resets because people know how to them - take whitetower - how many players solved it when it first came out - a few nowlook around and many have irt cause the solnt is out - first hand experienceon that quest - takes roughly 3 days to solve to the point that you can take ththe next day and go through the hole quest to do it - it is so spread out that is tough to do ... thus you have to take the time to put all of the pieces together and consideringhow purely goldsun's english is and his syntex the quest becomes evenharder - so you tell me how any under lvl 29 can even do that questwithout a solution becaues it _requies_ a hell of a lot of knowledgeon the game and where everything is!!! Summary - puzzles stop cheaters - so put em in and put them inbunches -- that will stop such assine walk thoroughs of 8 or 10% questrating in a little over 10 mins!!!Apollo - the one sick of cheaters**just like to say that every single puzzle quest out there has people cheating on, in fact I have seen more people cheat on the puzzle quests, like Dmitri and ganja, etc.......Tanis**Some puzzles can be cheated...like I said in my first note, two of thepuzzles can be somewhat scripted.  One can be entirely scripted, thoughits somewhat long (16 moves).  Another can be scripted so a player can compare results to a table, and theother just relies on logic and skill, since its randomized each time.The other thing I was hoping to do , in an effort to make questscheat-proof, is to create a library of short puzzles, maybe 9 or 10,and just have the quest be random combinations of them.  Given the factthat a player can't predict which puzzle will show up, it makes it reallyhard to cheat, and I doubt few people would go through the trouble of doingthe quest over and over to solve all the puzzles, for the sole purposeof providing others with the answers (and if they do, just make morepuzzles).  The bright side of all this is that it isn't that unfair either,My quest doesn't require people to travel to strange places in totally unrelated areas of the mud, all the puzzles are self-contained,and require no prior knowledge or special items.  They're just funand challenging puzzles for people of all levels to solve, and if you try the quest out, you'll see it has a little story line too...-K-  sick of cheaters, overpowered guilds, invulnerable monsters, etc...**post re:kawaiOk, I just hope the puzzles will have to do with the context of a fantasy world, relevant to the game :*)tanis**Hey I'm not against puzzles....I just don't think that puzzles can solvethe problem of cheating.Once again: If you make a quest ENJOYABLE...(with or without puzzles itreally doesn't matter) players will not cheat this much.Just try to think guys ... :) The MUD is extremely big. Quests are very difficult to solve sometimes. Some quests could be done by more players ata time. Some of the quest object could 'fade away' when you drop them orjust want to put them into a sack....(i.e. Shao Kahn quest > dolls) Thereare absolutely not enough hints and clues for the solutions etc. etc.So even though some players would like to solve a quest by themselves they always have to face these kind of difficulties...so they usually decide on cheating. (If you know what I mean... :) )In my oppinion, well designed and structured puzzles are cool...but they just cannot offer solution to our problem...ThormP.S.: if you need assistance let me now...I can take a look at your questand tell what I'd change... :) **I really like the 'Help Yorel' quests method of only letting 1 player work onthe quest at a time. If this is applies to more quests, then if someone decidesthat they need to work on it, and someone is already doing the quest, at leastit might be at least expected that some quest objects are missing.Oh, well. I'm not going to get too caught up in this one. Me.**Well the idea is cool...cooler than nothing at least.But quests do need to be changed...I still offer you my help...Your Thormy** I finished the coding of my quest. I would be glad if it will be added so if you can add it read the file /p/sed/quests/free_promet.doc There is more info about it. If you will have any que